                "file_text": "# Dhrit Platform - Agent Training Guide\n\nThis directory contains comprehensive training guides for all 8 specialized agents in the Dhrit platform.\n\n## Training Workflow\n\n### 1. Save Training Data\nUse the training commands from each agent's guide to save domain knowledge:\n\n```bash\n# Example for Kalp\ntrain-domain --agentName \"kalp\" --trainingContent \"DOMAIN TRAINING - KALP...\"\n```\n\n### 2. Train Agent\nTrain the agent with saved data:\n\n```bash\n# Example for Kalp\nkalp --mode \"train\"\n```\n\n### 3. Execute Tasks\nUse the trained agent for specific tasks:\n\n```bash\n# Example for Kalp\nkalp --projectId \"project-name\" --task \"Create design system\" --requirements \"Your requirements\"\n```\n\n## Available Agents\n\n### Core Development Agents\n\n| Agent | Role | Training Guide | Specialization |\n|-------|------|----------------|----------------|\n| **Roop** (रूप) | Frontend Developer | [roop-training.md](./roop-training.md) | React, Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS |\n| **Mool** (मूल) | Backend Developer | [mool-training.md](./mool-training.md) | Node.js, tRPC, APIs, Authentication |\n| **Kosh** (कोश) | Database Admin | [kosh-training.md](./kosh-training.md) | PostgreSQL, Prisma, Schema Design |\n| **Dhar** (धार) | QA & DevOps | [dhar-training.md](./dhar-training.md) | Testing, CI/CD, Deployment |\n\n### Enterprise Specialists\n\n| Agent | Role | Training Guide | Specialization |\n|-------|------|----------------|----------------|\n| **Kalp** (कल्प) | Design System | [kalp-training.md](./kalp-training.md) | Design Tokens, Components, Brand Identity |\n| **Bandh** (बंध) | Security | [bandh-training.md](./bandh-training.md) | Security Audits, Compliance, Vulnerability |\n| **Gati** (गति) | Performance | [gati-training.md](./gati-training.md) | Optimization, Caching, Load Testing |\n| **Pal** (पाल) | Architecture | [pal-training.md](./pal-training.md) | System Design, Microservices, Scalability |\n\n## Training All Agents\n\n### Quick Training Script\n```bash\n# Train all agents sequentially\nfor agent in kalp pal bandh roop mool kosh gati dhar; do\n  echo \"Training $agent...\"\n  $agent --mode \"train\"\ndone\n```\n\n### Bulk Training Command\n```bash\n# Use the bulk training tool\ntrain-all-agents\n```\n\n## Agent Coordination\n\nThe agents are designed to work together:\n\n1. **Pal** designs the overall architecture\n2. **Kalp** creates the design system\n3. **Bandh** establishes security requirements\n4. **Kosh** designs the database schema\n5. **Mool** builds the backend APIs\n6. **Roop** creates the frontend interface\n7. **Gati** optimizes performance\n8. **Dhar** tests and deploys\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Training Order\n1. **Foundation Agents**: Pal → Kalp → Bandh\n2. **Infrastructure Agents**: Kosh → Mool\n3. **Interface Agents**: Roop\n4. **Optimization Agents**: Gati → Dhar\n\n### Quality Assurance\n- Each agent should be trained with comprehensive domain knowledge\n- Test agents with simple tasks before complex projects\n- Ensure agents understand coordination protocols\n- Regularly update training content based on new technologies\n\n### Documentation\n- Keep training content updated with latest best practices\n- Document successful agent interactions and patterns\n- Maintain examples of high-quality agent outputs\n- Share learnings across the development team\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n- **Agent not responding**: Check if training was completed successfully\n- **Poor quality output**: Review and update training content\n- **Coordination issues**: Ensure all agents understand their roles and dependencies\n\n### Support\n- Review individual agent training guides for specific issues\n- Check the main project documentation for architecture details\n- Consult the development workflow guide for best practices",
