                "file_text": "# Dhrit Platform - Agent Communication Protocols\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Dhrit platform uses a sophisticated multi-agent coordination system where 8 specialized agents work together to build enterprise applications. This document defines the communication protocols, handoff procedures, and coordination patterns.\n\n## Agent Coordination Flow\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[User Requirements] --> B[Pal - Architecture]\n    B --> C[Kalp - Design System]\n    B --> D[Bandh - Security Planning]\n    \n    C --> E[Kosh - Database Design]\n    D --> E\n    B --> E\n    \n    E --> F[Mool - Backend APIs]\n    C --> F\n    D --> F\n    \n    F --> G[Roop - Frontend UI]\n    C --> G\n    \n    G --> H[Gati - Performance Optimization]\n    F --> H\n    E --> H\n    \n    H --> I[Dhar - Testing & Deployment]\n    G --> I\n    F --> I\n    E --> I\n    \n    I --> J[Production Application]\n```\n\n## Protocol Types\n\n### 1. Sequential Handoff Protocol\n**Used for**: Dependencies where one agent must complete before another starts\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Pal as Pal (Architecture)\n    participant Kalp as Kalp (Design)\n    participant Kosh as Kosh (Database)\n    participant Mool as Mool (Backend)\n    participant Roop as Roop (Frontend)\n    \n    Pal->>Kalp: Architecture constraints\n    Kalp->>Kalp: Create design system\n    Kalp->>Kosh: Design data requirements\n    Kalp->>Mool: Design tokens & APIs needed\n    Kosh->>Kosh: Design database schema\n    Kosh->>Mool: Database schema & models\n    Mool->>Mool: Build APIs\n    Mool->>Roop: API specifications\n    Kalp->>Roop: Design tokens & components\n    Roop->>Roop: Build frontend\n```\n\n### 2. Parallel Coordination Protocol\n**Used for**: Independent work that needs synchronization points\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[Requirements] --> B[Pal - Architecture]\n    B --> C[Bandh - Security]\n    B --> D[Gati - Performance]\n    B --> E[Kalp - Design]\n    \n    C --> F[Security Requirements]\n    D --> G[Performance Requirements]\n    E --> H[Design System]\n    \n    F --> I[Implementation Phase]\n    G --> I\n    H --> I\n```\n\n### 3. Feedback Loop Protocol\n**Used for**: Iterative improvement and optimization\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Initial Implementation] --> B[Gati - Performance Analysis]\n    B --> C{Performance OK?}\n    C -->|No| D[Optimization Recommendations]\n    D --> E[Roop/Mool - Apply Optimizations]\n    E --> A\n    C -->|Yes| F[Dhar - Quality Testing]\n    F --> G{Tests Pass?}\n    G -->|No| H[Bug Reports & Fixes]\n    H --> E\n    G -->|Yes| I[Production Ready]\n```\n\n## Communication Standards\n\n### Message Format\n```json\n{\n  \"messageId\": \"uuid\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"ISO-8601\",\n  \"fromAgent\": \"kalp\",\n  \"toAgent\": \"roop\",\n  \"messageType\": \"handoff|request|response|notification\",\n  \"priority\": \"high|medium|low\",\n  \"projectId\": \"project-identifier\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"action\": \"design_tokens_ready\",\n    \"data\": {},\n    \"requirements\": [],\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"blockers\": []\n  },\n  \"status\": \"pending|in_progress|completed|failed\"\n}\n```\n\n### Agent Status Codes\n- `READY` - Agent is available for work\n- `WORKING` - Agent is actively processing\n- `BLOCKED` - Agent is waiting for dependencies\n- `COMPLETED` - Agent has finished current task\n- `ERROR` - Agent encountered an error\n- `REVIEWING` - Agent is reviewing another agent's work\n\n## Detailed Protocol Specifications\n\n### 1. Architecture → Design Handoff (Pal → Kalp)\n\n**Trigger**: Project requirements received\n**Protocol**: Sequential Handoff\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Pal\n    participant Kalp\n    participant Redis\n    \n    User->>Pal: Project requirements\n    Pal->>Pal: Analyze & design architecture\n    Pal->>Redis: Store architecture decisions\n    Pal->>Kalp: Architecture constraints\n    Note over Kalp: Design system must align with architecture\n    Kalp->>Kalp: Create design system\n    Kalp->>Redis: Store design tokens\n    Kalp->>Pal: Design system complete\n```\n\n**Handoff Data**:\n- System architecture diagrams\n- Technology stack decisions\n- Scalability requirements\n- Integration patterns\n- Performance targets\n\n### 2. Design → Development Handoff (Kalp → Roop/Mool)\n\n**Trigger**: Design system completion\n**Protocol**: Parallel Distribution\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Kalp\n    participant Roop\n    participant Mool\n    participant Redis\n    \n    Kalp->>Redis: Publish design tokens\n    Redis->>Roop: Design tokens available\n    Redis->>Mool: API design requirements\n    \n    par Frontend Implementation\n        Roop->>Roop: Implement components\n        Roop->>Redis: Component library ready\n    and Backend Implementation\n        Mool->>Mool: Build APIs\n        Mool->>Redis: API endpoints ready\n    end\n    \n    Redis->>Kalp: Implementation status\n```\n\n**Handoff Data**:\n- Design tokens (colors, typography, spacing)\n- Component specifications\n- Layout patterns\n- Animation guidelines\n- API design requirements\n\n### 3. Database → Backend Handoff (Kosh → Mool)\n\n**Trigger**: Database schema completion\n**Protocol**: Sequential Handoff with Validation\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Kosh\n    participant Mool\n    participant Bandh\n    participant Redis\n    \n    Kosh->>Kosh: Design database schema\n    Kosh->>Bandh: Security review request\n    Bandh->>Bandh: Review schema security\n    Bandh->>Kosh: Security approval/changes\n    Kosh->>Redis: Store final schema\n    Kosh->>Mool: Database schema ready\n    Mool->>Mool: Generate Prisma models\n    Mool->>Redis: Models generated\n```\n\n**Handoff Data**:\n- Database schema definitions\n- Prisma models\n- Migration scripts\n- Indexing strategies\n- Security policies\n\n### 4. Performance Optimization Protocol (Gati ↔ All Agents)\n\n**Trigger**: Performance thresholds not met\n**Protocol**: Feedback Loop with Prioritization\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Gati - Performance Monitoring] --> B{Performance Issues?}\n    B -->|Yes| C[Analyze Bottlenecks]\n    C --> D{Frontend Issues?}\n    C --> E{Backend Issues?}\n    C --> F{Database Issues?}\n    \n    D -->|Yes| G[Roop - Optimize Frontend]\n    E -->|Yes| H[Mool - Optimize Backend]\n    F -->|Yes| I[Kosh - Optimize Database]\n    \n    G --> J[Re-test Performance]\n    H --> J\n    I --> J\n    \n    J --> A\n    B -->|No| K[Performance Acceptable]\n```\n\n### 5. Quality Assurance Protocol (Dhar ↔ All Agents)\n\n**Trigger**: Code/component completion\n**Protocol**: Multi-stage Validation\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Agent as Any Agent\n    participant Dhar\n    participant Redis\n    participant Bandh\n    \n    Agent->>Redis: Work completed\n    Redis->>Dhar: Trigger QA process\n    \n    Dhar->>Dhar: Run automated tests\n    Dhar->>Bandh: Security scan request\n    Bandh->>Bandh: Security analysis\n    Bandh->>Dhar: Security results\n    \n    alt Tests Pass\n        Dhar->>Redis: QA approved\n        Redis->>Agent: Ready for next phase\n    else Tests Fail\n        Dhar->>Agent: Issues found\n        Agent->>Agent: Fix issues\n        Agent->>Redis: Fixes completed\n        Redis->>Dhar: Re-test request\n    end\n```\n\n## Enhanced Protocol Features\n\n### 1. Smart Dependency Resolution\n```javascript\n// Automatic dependency tracking\nconst dependencies = {\n  roop: ['kalp', 'mool'], // Frontend needs design tokens and APIs\n  mool: ['kosh', 'bandh'], // Backend needs database and security\n  gati: ['roop', 'mool', 'kosh'], // Performance needs all implementations\n  dhar: ['*'] // QA needs everything\n};\n```\n\n### 2. Conflict Resolution Protocol\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Conflict Detected] --> B{Conflict Type?}\n    B -->|Resource| C[Resource Arbitration]\n    B -->|Technical| D[Technical Review]\n    B -->|Priority| E[Priority Resolution]\n    \n    C --> F[Pal - Architecture Decision]\n    D --> G[Senior Agent Review]\n    E --> H[User/PM Decision]\n    \n    F --> I[Resolution Applied]\n    G --> I\n    H --> I\n```\n\n### 3. Real-time Status Broadcasting\n```javascript\n// Redis pub/sub for real-time updates\nconst statusUpdate = {\n  agent: 'kalp',\n  status: 'COMPLETED',\n  task: 'design_system_creation',\n  progress: 100,\n  nextAgents: ['roop', 'mool'],\n  blockers: [],\n  estimatedCompletion: null\n};\n```\n\n### 4. Quality Gates\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[Agent Work] --> B{Quality Gate}\n    B -->|Pass| C[Next Phase]\n    B -->|Fail| D[Return to Agent]\n    D --> E[Fix Issues]\n    E --> A\n    \n    B --> F[Automated Tests]\n    B --> G[Security Scan]\n    B --> H[Performance Check]\n    B --> I[Code Review]\n```\n\n## Protocol Enhancements\n\n### 1. Predictive Coordination\n- **AI-powered scheduling** based on agent workload\n- **Bottleneck prediction** and proactive resource allocation\n- **Dependency optimization** to minimize wait times\n\n### 2. Adaptive Protocols\n- **Learning from past projects** to optimize handoff timing\n- **Dynamic priority adjustment** based on project urgency\n- **Context-aware communication** based on project type\n\n### 3. Rollback Mechanisms\n- **Version control** for all agent outputs\n- **Rollback triggers** when downstream agents detect issues\n- **Cascade rollback** prevention with impact analysis\n\n### 4. Performance Metrics\n- **Handoff latency** tracking\n- **Agent utilization** monitoring\n- **Protocol efficiency** measurement\n- **Bottleneck identification** and resolution\n\n## Implementation in Redis\n\n### Message Queues\n```\ndhrit:queue:kalp:incoming\ndhrit:queue:kalp:outgoing\ndhrit:status:kalp\ndhrit:dependencies:project-id\ndhrit:handoffs:active\n```\n\n### Status Tracking\n```\ndhrit:project:{projectId}:status\ndhrit:project:{projectId}:agents\ndhrit:project:{projectId}:timeline\ndhrit:project:{projectId}:blockers\n```\n\nThis protocol system ensures efficient, reliable, and scalable coordination between all 8 agents while maintaining quality and performance standards.",
