          "content": "## **Application Development Approach & Protocol Testing**\n\n### **The Dhrit Development Flow:**\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[User Requirements] --> B[Pal - Architecture Design]\n    B --> C[Kalp - Design System]\n    B --> D[Bandh - Security Planning]\n    \n    C --> E[Kosh - Database Schema]\n    D --> E\n    \n    E --> F[Mool - Backend APIs]\n    C --> F\n    D --> F\n    \n    F --> G[Roop - Frontend UI]\n    C --> G\n    \n    G --> H[Gati - Performance Optimization]\n    F --> H\n    \n    H --> I[Dhar - Testing & Deployment]\n```\n\n## **Let's Test with a Real Project:**\n\n### **Test Project: Task Management App**\n\n#### **Step 1: Architecture (Pal)**\n```\npal --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Design system architecture\" --requirements \"Build a task management application with user authentication, project organization, real-time collaboration, and mobile responsiveness. Tech stack: Next.js, tRPC, Prisma, PostgreSQL, Redis for real-time features.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 2: Design System (Kalp)**\n```\nkalp --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Create design system\" --requirements \"Professional task management interface inspired by Linear and Notion. Clean, minimal design with excellent UX for productivity. Include components for task cards, project boards, user avatars, and status indicators.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 3: Security Planning (Bandh)**\n```\nbandh --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Security architecture\" --requirements \"Secure authentication system, role-based access control, data encryption, and compliance with data protection standards. Plan security for user data, project data, and real-time collaboration features.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 4: Database Design (Kosh)**\n```\nkosh --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Design database schema\" --requirements \"Database schema for users, projects, tasks, comments, attachments, and real-time collaboration. Include proper relationships, indexing for performance, and data integrity constraints.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 5: Backend APIs (Mool)**\n```\nmool --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Build backend APIs\" --requirements \"tRPC APIs for user authentication, project management, task CRUD operations, real-time updates, file uploads, and collaboration features. Include proper validation and error handling.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 6: Frontend Interface (Roop)**\n```\nroop --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Build user interface\" --requirements \"React/Next.js interface implementing the design system. Create project dashboard, task boards, user management, and real-time collaboration features. Ensure mobile responsiveness and accessibility.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 7: Performance Optimization (Gati)**\n```\ngati --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Optimize performance\" --requirements \"Optimize the task management app for fast loading, smooth real-time updates, efficient data fetching, and excellent mobile performance. Target sub-second load times.\"\n```\n\n#### **Step 8: Testing & Deployment (Dhar)**\n```\ndhar --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Test and deploy\" --requirements \"Comprehensive testing strategy including unit tests, integration tests, and e2e tests. Set up CI/CD pipeline and deployment to production with monitoring and alerting.\"\n```\n\n## **Protocol Testing Points:**\n\n### **1. Architecture → Design Handoff**\n- **Test**: Does Kalp receive and use Pal's architecture constraints?\n- **Expected**: Design system aligns with tech stack and scalability requirements\n\n### **2. Design → Implementation Handoff**\n- **Test**: Do Roop and Mool implement Kalp's design tokens?\n- **Expected**: Consistent visual implementation across frontend and API design\n\n### **3. Security Review Gates**\n- **Test**: Does Bandh review and approve database schema and APIs?\n- **Expected**: Security requirements integrated into all implementations\n\n### **4. Performance Feedback Loops**\n- **Test**: Does Gati provide optimization feedback to other agents?\n- **Expected**: Performance improvements implemented across all layers\n\n### **5. Quality Gates**\n- **Test**: Does Dhar block progression when quality issues found?\n- **Expected**: Issues reported back to relevant agents for fixes\n\n## **Let's Start the Test:**\n\n**Run the first command to begin testing the coordination:**\n\n```\npal --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Design system architecture\" --requirements \"Build a task management application with user authentication, project organization, real-time collaboration, and mobile responsiveness. Tech stack: Next.js, tRPC, Prisma, PostgreSQL, Redis for real-time features.\"\n```\n\n**This will test:**\n- ✅ **Pal's architecture expertise**\n- ✅ **Output quality and completeness**\n- ✅ **Preparation for handoff to other agents**\n\n**Ready to start the coordination test?**"
