oling (100 connections)\n- Redis caching for frequently accessed data\n- CDN for static assets\n- Horizontal scaling ready with load balancers\n\n🔒 SECURITY ARCHITECTURE:\n- JWT tokens with refresh mechanism\n- Role-based access control (RBAC)\n- API rate limiting (100 req/min per user)\n- Input validation and sanitization\n\n📁 Output saved to: /dhrit/projects/taskmaster/architecture/design-system-architecture-1735766636.json\n\n🔄 Project Status: Use 'status --projectId \"taskmaster\"' to see coordination status\n```\n\n### **Step 3: Design System (Kalp)**\n```bash\nkalp --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Create design system\" --requirements \"Professional task management interface inspired by Linear and Notion. Clean, minimal design with excellent UX for productivity. Include components for task cards, project boards, user avatars, status indicators, and real-time collaboration features. Color scheme: Modern blues and grays with accent colors for priorities.\"\n```\n\n**Expected Output:**\n```\n✅ KALP Agent Result:\n\nDESIGN SYSTEM - TASKMASTER\n\n🎨 DESIGN TOKENS:\nColors:\n- Primary: #2563eb (Blue 600) for actions and focus\n- Secondary: #64748b (Slate 500) for secondary elements  \n- Success: #10b981 (Emerald 500) for completed tasks\n- Warning: #f59e0b (Amber 500) for in-progress\n- Error: #ef4444 (Red 500) for urgent/overdue\n- Neutral: #f8fafc to #0f172a (Slate scale)\n\nTypography:\n- Font: Inter (system fallback: -apple-system, sans-serif)\n- Headings: 600-700 weight, tight line-height\n- Body: 400-500 weight, relaxed line-height\n- Code: JetBrains Mono for technical content\n\n🧩 COMPONENT SPECIFICATIONS:\n1. TaskCard: Compact card with title, assignee, due date, priority indicator\n2. ProjectBoard: Kanban-style columns with drag-and-drop\n3. UserAvatar: Circular avatar with online status indicator\n4. StatusBadge: Pill-shaped status with color coding\n5. PriorityIcon: Triangle indicators (High/Medium/Low)\n6. CommentThread: Nested comments with timestamps\n7. NavigationSidebar: Collapsible sidebar with project tree\n\n📱 RESPONSIVE DESIGN:\n- Mobile-first approach\n- Breakpoints: sm(640px), md(768px), lg(1024px), xl(1280px)\n- Touch-friendly targets (44px minimum)\n- Swipe gestures for mobile task management\n\n✨ MICRO-INTERACTIONS:\n- Smooth hover states (150ms transitions)\n- Task completion animations\n- Real-time typing indicators\n- Drag-and-drop visual feedback\n\n📁 Output saved to: /dhrit/projects/taskmaster/design/create-design-system-1735766696.json\n\n🔄 Project Status: Use 'status --projectId \"taskmaster\"' to see coordination status\n```\n\n### **Step 4: Security Planning (Bandh)**\n```bash\nbandh --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Security architecture\" --requirements \"Secure authentication system, role-based access control, data encryption, and compliance with data protection standards. Plan security for user data, project data, and real-time collaboration features. Include API security, input validation, and audit logging.\"\n```\n\n**Expected Output:**\n```\n✅ BANDH Agent Result:\n\nSECURITY ARCHITECTURE - TASKMASTER\n\n🔒 AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION:\n- NextAuth.js with multiple providers (Google, GitHub, Email)\n- JWT tokens with 15-minute access, 7-day refresh\n- Role-based access control: Admin, Manager, Member, Viewer\n- Project-level permissions with inheritance\n- Session management with secure httpOnly cookies\n\n🛡️ DATA PROTECTION:\n- Encryption at rest: AES-256 for sensitive data\n- Encryption in transit: TLS 1.3 for all connections\n- Database field-level encryption for PII\n- Redis encryption for cached session data\n- File upload scanning for malware\n\n🔍 API SECURITY:\n- Rate limiting: 100 requests/minute per user\n- Input validation with Zod schemas\n- SQL injection prevention via Prisma\n- XSS protection with Content Security Policy\n- CORS configuration for allowed origins\n\n📊 AUDIT & COMPLIANCE:\n- Comprehensive audit logging for all actions\n- GDPR compliance with data export/deletion\n- SOC 2 Type II preparation checklist\n- Regular security scans and penetration testing\n- Incident response procedures\n\n🚨 MONITORING & ALERTS:\n- Failed login attempt monitoring\n- Unusual access pattern detection\n- Real-time security event alerts\n- Automated threat response procedures\n\n📁 Output saved to: /dhrit/projects/taskmaster/security/security-architecture-1735766756.json\n\n🔄 Project Status: Use 'status --projectId \"taskmaster\"' to see coordination status\n```\n\n### **Step 5: Database Design (Kosh)**\n```bash\nkosh --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Design database schema\" --requirements \"Database schema for users, projects, tasks, comments, attachments, and real-time collaboration. Include proper relationships, indexing for performance, data integrity constraints, and support for role-based access control. Optimize for 1000+ concurrent users.\"\n```\n\n**Expected Output:**\n```\n✅ KOSH Agent Result:\n\nDATABASE SCHEMA - TASKMASTER\n\n🗄️ CORE ENTITIES:\nUsers: id, email, name, avatar, role, createdAt, updatedAt\nProjects: id, name, description, ownerId, status, createdAt, updatedAt\nTasks: id, title, description, projectId, assigneeId, status, priority, dueDate\nComments: id, content, taskId, authorId, createdAt, updatedAt\nAttachments: id, filename, url, size, taskId, uploadedBy, createdAt\n\n🔗 RELATIONSHIPS:\n- Users ↔ Projects (many-to-many via ProjectMembers)\n- Projects → Tasks (one-to-many)\n- Users → Tasks (one-to-many for assignments)\n- Tasks → Comments (one-to-many)\n- Tasks → Attachments (one-to-many)\n\n⚡ PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATIONS:\nIndexes:\n- Users: email (unique), role\n- Projects: ownerId, status, createdAt\n- Tasks: projectId, assigneeId, status, priority, dueDate\n- Comments: taskId, authorId, createdAt\n- ProjectMembers: userId, projectId (composite unique)\n\n🔒 SECURITY CONSTRAINTS:\n- Row-level security for multi-tenant data isolation\n- Soft deletes for audit trail preservation\n- Encrypted fields for sensitive data\n- Foreign key constraints for data integrity\n\n📊 SCALABILITY FEATURES:\n- Connection pooling (max 100 connections)\n- Read replicas for query distribution\n- Partitioning strategy for large tables\n- Automated backup and point-in-time recovery\n\n📁 Output saved to: /dhrit/projects/taskmaster/database/design-database-schema-1735766816.json\n\n🔄 Project Status: Use 'status --projectId \"taskmaster\"' to see coordination status\n```\n\n### **Step 6: Backend APIs (Mool)**\n```bash\nmool --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Build backend APIs\" --requirements \"tRPC APIs for user authentication, project management, task CRUD operations, real-time updates, file uploads, and collaboration features. Include proper validation, error handling, and integration with the database schema and security requirements.\"\n```\n\n**Expected Output:**\n```\n✅ MOOL Agent Result:\n\nBACKEND APIS - TASKMASTER\n\n🔌 tRPC API STRUCTURE:\nAuthentication Router:\n- auth.login(email, password) → JWT tokens\n- auth.register(userData) → User creation\n- auth.refresh(refreshToken) → New access token\n- auth.logout() → Token invalidation\n\nProject Router:\n- project.create(projectData) → New project\n- project.list() → User's projects with permissions\n- project.get(projectId) → Project details\n- project.update(projectId, data) → Project modification\n- project.delete(projectId) → Soft delete project\n- project.addMember(projectId, userId, role) → Team management\n\nTask Router:\n- task.create(taskData) → New task\n- task.list(projectId, filters) → Filtered task list\n- task.get(taskId) → Task details with comments\n- task.update(taskId, data) → Task modification\n- task.delete(taskId) → Soft delete task\n- task.assign(taskId, userId) → Task assignment\n\nReal-time Router:\n- realtime.subscribe(projectId) → WebSocket connection\n- realtime.broadcast(projectId, event) → Live updates\n- realtime.typing(taskId, isTyping) → Typing indicators\n\n🔒 SECURITY IMPLEMENTATION:\n- JWT middleware for protected routes\n- Role-based access control checks\n- Input validation with Zod schemas\n- Rate limiting per endpoint\n- Audit logging for all mutations\n\n⚡ PERFORMANCE FEATURES:\n- Database query optimization\n- Redis caching for frequent queries\n- Pagination for large datasets\n- Background job processing\n- Connection pooling\n\n📁 Output saved to: /dhrit/projects/taskmaster/backend/build-backend-apis-1735766876.json\n\n🔄 Project Status: Use 'status --projectId \"taskmaster\"' to see coordination status\n```\n\n### **Step 7: Frontend Interface (Roop)**\n```bash\nroop --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Build user interface\" --requirements \"React/Next.js interface implementing the design system. Create project dashboard, task boards, user management, and real-time collaboration features. Ensure mobile responsiveness, accessibility, and integration with the tRPC APIs. Include drag-and-drop functionality and real-time updates.\"\n```\n\n**Expected Output:**\n```\n✅ ROOP Agent Result:\n\nFRONTEND INTERFACE - TASKMASTER\n\n🖥️ PAGE STRUCTURE:\n/dashboard - Project overview with recent tasks\n/projects/[id] - Kanban board with drag-and-drop\n/projects/[id]/tasks/[taskId] - Task detail modal\n/settings - User profile and preferences\n/auth/login - Authentication pages\n/auth/register - User registration\n\n🧩 COMPONENT IMPLEMENTATION:\nTaskBoard.tsx:\n- Kanban columns with @dnd-kit for drag-and-drop\n- Real-time updates via tRPC subscriptions\n- Optimistic updates for smooth UX\n- Virtual scrolling for large task lists\n\nTaskCard.tsx:\n- Compact design with priority indicators\n- User avatars with online status\n- Due date highlighting and overdue alerts\n- Quick actions (assign, priority, status)\n\nProjectSidebar.tsx:\n- Collapsible navigation\n- Project switching with search\n- Team member list with roles\n- Real-time activity feed\n\n🔄 REAL-TIME FEATURES:\n- WebSocket integration for live updates\n- Typing indicators in comments\n- Live cursor tracking for collaboration\n- Instant task status changes\n- Push notifications for assignments\n\n📱 RESPONSIVE DESIGN:\n- Mobile-first CSS with Tailwind\n- Touch gestures for task management\n- Responsive navigation patterns\n- Optimized for tablets and phones\n\n♿ ACCESSIBILITY:\n- WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\n- Keyboard navigation support\n- Screen reader optimization\n- High contrast mode support\n- Focus management for modals\n\n📁 Output saved to: /dhrit/projects/taskmaster/frontend/build-user-interface-1735766936.json\n\n🔄 Project Status: Use 'status --projectId \"taskmaster\"' to see coordination status\n```\n\n### **Step 8: Performance Optimization (Gati)**\n```bash\ngati --projectId \"taskmaster\" --task \"Optimize performance\" --requirements \"Optimize the task management app for fast loading, smooth real-time updates, efficient data fetching, and excellent mobile performance. Target sub-second load times, 60fps animations, and efficient memory usage.\"\n```\n\n**Expected Output:**\n```\n✅ GATI Agent Result:\n\nPERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION - TASKMASTER\n\n⚡ FRONTEND OPTIMIZATIONS:\nBundle Optimization:\n- Code splitting by route and feature\n- Dynamic imports for heavy components\n- Tree shaking to remove unused code\n- Bundle size target: <200KB initial load\n\nImage & Asset Optimization:\n- Next.js Image component with WebP/AVIF\n- Lazy loading for non-critical images\n- CDN integration for static assets\n- Responsive image sizing\n\nCaching Strategy:\n- Service worker for offline functionality\n- Browser caching for static resources\n- SWR for client-side data caching\n- Optimistic updates for instant feedback\n\n🔧 BACKEND OPTIMIZATIONS:\nDatabase Performance:\n- Query optimization with proper indexes\n- Connection pooling (max 100 connections)\n- Read replicas for query distribution\n- Database query caching with Redis\n\nAPI Optimizations:\n- Response compression (gzip/brotli)\n- Pagination for large datasets\n- Batch operations for bulk updates\n- Background job processing\n\n📊 MO